{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"spodumene-stoned-arkshell","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Build the one-time strip as a committed operational script, and prove it on a scratch clone before\nany window. **No new dependency**: `git-filter-repo` is deliberately not used. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why stock plumbing\n`git fast-export --no-data --signed-tags=strip --export-marks=old.marks tickets` | filter |\n`git fast-import --export-marks=new.marks`. Verified on the real branch: the stream carries\n`M 100644 <sha> <path>` with **zero** inline blob data (26 MB stream for ~49,900 commits), so the\nfilter is line-oriented text processing that never moves the ~1 GiB. No `deleteall`; no tags in a\nbranch export (so `--signed-tags=strip` is a harmless no-op); merges ride `merge :n`; **empty commits\nare kept**, so DAG topology and every file's introduction point survive — which is exactly what\nancestry-based authorship verification needs. filter-repo would prune them and reshape the graph.\n\n**Proven result:** 1,172,586,762 -> 98,803,422 bytes (8.4%), all commits and all merge commits\npreserved, HEAD tree byte-identical except the intended paths, ~30 s end to end.\n\n## Required corrections (each was a real defect found in review)\n1. Must run in a fresh **UNFILTERED** clone — `fast-import` hard-fails `fatal: blob not found` in a\n   `blob:none` partial clone, and this host's `origin` is one.\n2. Strip **both** `.bridge_state/` **and** `.bridge_state.bak-retarget/` prefixes — B6 removes the\n   latter at HEAD only; its 33 MB stays in history.\n3. **Derive the re-add set DYNAMICALLY** — `git ls-tree -r --name-only <old-tip> -- .bridge_state/` —\n   never a hardcoded list. It is three files today but **A2-1 adds `get_rotation.json`**, so at window\n   time it is four; a hardcoded list would fail the tree-identity assertion.\n4. The filter must be **`data <n>`-length-aware**, not `grep -v`: commit messages live inside `data`\n   blocks. (Today 0 of ~49,900 messages begin with `M `/`D `, but the script must not rely on that.)\n5. Push with **`--force-with-lease`**, never `--force` — the remote tip moves constantly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] On a scratch unfiltered clone, the script produces a rewritten branch whose **commit count and\n      merge-commit count are unchanged** (measured at run time, not hardcoded). Tier: **repo-level\n      assertion in the dry-run harness**.\n- [ ] `rev-parse <new-tip>^{tree}` **equals** the old tip tree after the dynamic re-add. Tier:\n      **repo-level assertion**. This is the \"not one byte of live content changed\" invariant.\n- [ ] The re-add set is discovered from `ls-tree`, proven by a fixture where a 4th `.bridge_state`\n      file exists. Tier: **integration** with a synthetic 4-file store.\n- [ ] Pack size drops to <=15% of the original. Tier: **repo-level measurement**.\n- [ ] The filter preserves a commit message that begins with `M ` (adversarial fixture). Tier:\n      **unit** on the stream filter.\n- [ ] The script refuses to run in a partial clone, with a clear message. Tier: **integration**\n      against a `--filter=blob:none` clone.\n- [ ] All assertions run **before** any push; the script has no push step of its own.\n\n## Files\n`infra/scripts/reclaim-bridge-history.sh` (or `.py`), dry-run harness, tests\n\nScope: M. No code dependencies; must exist before A6-1.","id":"6d50-8449-e71a-45b4","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"A6-0c: build and dry-run the history-strip script using stock git plumbing"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785372525332671001,"uuid":"c9a986a4-821e-4698-95a7-433248504e04"}